@@ -0,0 +1,203 @@
+**PENDING FINAL LOAO CELLS — do not cite this line.**
+
+`DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`
+
+## Structural result before model statistics
+
+[RUN] The exact bounded catalogue contains 36,788 candidates at 37 anchors.
+The coalition-size distribution is:
+
+| `|A|` | rows | share of full catalogue |
+|---:|---:|---:|
+| 0 | 37 | 0.101% |
+| 1 | 28,960 | 78.721% |
+| 2 | 7,104 | 19.311% |
+| 3 | 292 | 0.794% |
+| 4 | 177 | 0.481% |
+| 5 | 125 | 0.340% |
+| 6 | 4 | 0.011% |
+| 7 | 12 | 0.033% |
+| 8 | 3 | 0.008% |
+| 100 | 74 | 0.201% |
+
+[DERIVED] Empty sets and singletons are 28,997/36,788 = 78.822% of the
+full evaluation support. They are not optimizer rows: the declared head returns
+zero without calling its network for `|A| <= 1`. The actual scalar-fit support
+is 7,791 rows with `|A| >= 2`; 7,104/7,791 = 91.181% of those rows are pairs.
+Thus the full support is dominated by trivial structural zeros and even the
+nontrivial support is dominated by pairs. Full-support fit statistics cannot be
+read as broad evidence about large coalitions. I therefore report the requested
+full-catalogue metrics and an explicit `|A| >= 2` sensitivity beside them.
+
+[RUN] Before fitting, all 28,960 singleton targets were exactly zero (maximum
+absolute value `0.0`); all 37 empty targets were also exactly zero. The maximum
+absolute residual in the normalized identity
+`joint/kappa - additive/kappa - Psi_A/kappa` was `2.8422e-14` over all 36,788
+candidates.
+
+## Answer
+
+[RUN] PENDING FINAL PRIMARY METRICS.
+
+[INFERRED] PENDING FINAL CEILING INTERPRETATION.
+
+## Evidence labels and scope
+
+- `[RUN]` means verified by running the required interpreter against the current
+  exact-path code and generated rows.
+- `[DERIVED]` means arithmetic or algebra applied to run outputs and declarations.
+- `[INFERRED]` is the stated interpretation of those measurements.
+
+[RUN] This was a declared-target predictive-quality diagnostic only. It ran no
+production training, policy, acceptance test, or EE endpoint. Loss values are
+never evidence about EE, no loss is used as such here, and this report makes no
+EE claim. No sealed source, constant, schema, threshold, sign, seed, horizon,
+price, control law, or optimizer setting was changed.
+
+## Sealed v2 primary and v1 secondary
+
+[RUN] PENDING TABLE.
+
+[RUN] Every interval in the primary comparison is a 2,000-replicate percentile
+anchor-bootstrap interval. The bootstrap samples the 37 anchor sufficient
+statistics with replacement and reconstructs pooled metrics. LOAO uses one
+sealed learner seed. LOWO reports the arithmetic mean over the same four sealed
+seeds used by C1REAL. LOWO has only two world folds and is descriptive evidence
+about these two worlds, not a powered population-of-worlds estimate.
+
+## What the singleton mass does to the metrics
+
+[RUN] PENDING FULL/NONTRIVIAL TABLE.
+
+[DERIVED] The structure-aware constant is the fair constant floor for the
+declared object: it predicts exact zero at `|A| <= 1` and the training-fold mean
+on `|A| >= 2`. The unanchored literal-mean comparator is also shown to expose how
+much the hard anchor itself changes top-1 and ordering. PENDING INTERPRETATION.
+
+## References and empirical capacity ceiling
+
+[RUN] PENDING REFERENCE TABLES.
+
+[RUN] The linear reference standardizes each coordinate using outer-training
+rows, selects ridge from `{0.01,0.1,1,10,100,1000}` on training-only held-in
+anchors, and refits on the complete outer-training fold. The high-capacity
+reference is the C1REAL family adapted to scalar C3: standardized raw inputs
+plus fixed-seed `256,256` ReLU random features and an intercept, with the same
+training-only ridge grid. Both consume the same invariant vectors and receive
+the same hard-zero insertion at `|A| <= 1`.
+
+[RUN] The width screen preserves two ReLU hidden layers, 2,000 full-batch Adam
+epochs, learning rate `1e-3`, betas `(0.9,0.999)`, epsilon `1e-8`, zero weight
+decay, and direct scalar MSE. Width `(64,64)` is sealed; `(128,128)` is a
+diagnostic widening. PENDING WIDTH RESULT.
+
+[INFERRED] PENDING ARCHITECTURAL V INFORMATIONAL.
+
+## Same-sample exact construction
+
+[RUN] The modeled panel mirrors C1REALV2: world 1 steps 0–17 and world 2 steps
+0–18, 37 anchors total, setting `a-r0`, carrier `nearest-eligible`, 100 users,
+the shipped bounded catalogue, unchanged calibration, and boundary `(0,)`.
+Generation took mean `386.6643`, median `374.2304`, and range
+`329.4410`–`535.7481` seconds per anchor, including exact source and catalogue
+work.
+
+[RUN] For every generation process, the imported pilot module's
+`PILOT_PRIMITIVE_SOURCE_FALLBACK` began `True`, was set to `False` in-process
+before `_build_anchor_rows`, and was restored to `True` in `finally`. The
+bounded catalogue was then enumerated by `_catalogue_with_census`, and
+`_exact_interactions` supplied exact normalized `joint`, `additive`, and `Psi`
+values. Generation held and released one anchor's source/evaluator rows at a
+time. The catalogue census reports zero candidate-shortlist misses and zero
+shortlist-superset misses at every anchor.
+
+[RUN] A C3-specific construction correction was necessary. The declared route
+state is `_route_state(row, "C3") = (*row.q1_state, *row.q2_state)`, while the
+pilot `_coalition_context` currently places Q1 alone in each member. The fitted
+diagnostic contexts preserve that function's physical/resource fields but put
+Q1+Q2 into both selected and incumbent member states. V2 repairs both Q1 parts
+through `mcrl-v025-stagec-q1-action-v2` and leaves Q2 unchanged; v1 retains the
+original Q1+Q2. This is why the observed member widths are 80 (v2) and 82 (v1),
+and invariant-vector dimensions are 324 (v2) and 328 (v1).
+
+[RUN] Production `CoalitionRow` deliberately rejects `|A| < 2`. To evaluate the
+declared full support without inventing invalid production rows, compact
+diagnostic records carry exact targets/sizes for all candidates, while complete
+`CoalitionContext` vectors are constructed only for the 7,791 trainable rows.
+This is a genuine C3 deviation from C1's per-action row construction. C3 also
+uses direct scalar MSE rather than C1's pairwise/gauge objective; no C1 pair cap
+or gauge was imported.
+
+[RUN] Source generation used the sealed eight-action selection shortlist because
+that is the support consumed by the bounded catalogue; it did not generate the
+2,000 off-selection legal actions per anchor that the catalogue census records
+as outside support. This avoids off-support exact work without omitting a
+catalogue candidate: each anchor has zero selection-shortlist and superset
+misses. This differs from the source-only research note's conservative
+`full_legal_actions=True` suggestion, not from the fitted bounded support.
+
+## Learner and metric protocol
+
+[RUN] The sealed primary is the repository `AdamMLPHead` wrapped with the
+declared `AdamSetInteractionHead` hard-zero semantics: hidden `(64,64)`, ReLU,
+learning rate `1.0e-3`, Adam betas `(0.9,0.999)`, epsilon `1e-8`, zero weight
+decay, loss weight 1, 2,000 deterministic full-batch epochs, and no early
+selection. The diagnostic creates the standalone C3 network directly from each
+fold seed, matching C1REAL's diagnostic initialization convention; it does not
+advance a production orchestrator RNG through C1 and C2 initializations.
+
+[RUN] Level `R²` is pooled on raw held-out `Psi_A/kappa` values with no
+test-time re-gauging. Pairwise ordering uses all non-tied true candidate pairs
+within an anchor, truth ties within `1e-12` excluded and prediction ties within
+`1e-15` worth 0.5. Top-1 uses stable predicted argmax and credits any true
+maximum within `1e-12`. The sensitivity repeats all three after excluding
+`|A| <= 1`.
+
+## Permutation invariance
+
+[RUN] PENDING INVARIANCE RESULT. For every trainable context, member order was
+reversed before recomputing the declared invariant vector and the fitted head's
+score. The pre-fit invariant-vector maximum difference was `2.2737e-13`.
