@@ -0,0 +1,302 @@
+**On repaired v2, the sealed C3 head's LOAO ordering is `0.5484` (`0.5797` on `|A|>=2`), level `R²` is `-0.0685`, and top-1 is `0.3243` versus the anchor-respecting constant floor `0.2973`; the catalogue sizes are `{0:37, 1:28,960, 2:7,104, 3:292, 4:177, 5:125, 6:4, 7:12, 8:3, 100:74}`, and the empirical ceiling is mixed—architectural/optimization-limited for level calibration but informational-looking for coalition selection.**
+
+`DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`
+
+## Structural result before model statistics
+
+[RUN] The exact bounded catalogue contains 36,788 candidates at 37 anchors.
+The coalition-size distribution is:
+
+| `|A|` | rows | share of full catalogue |
+|---:|---:|---:|
+| 0 | 37 | 0.101% |
+| 1 | 28,960 | 78.721% |
+| 2 | 7,104 | 19.311% |
+| 3 | 292 | 0.794% |
+| 4 | 177 | 0.481% |
+| 5 | 125 | 0.340% |
+| 6 | 4 | 0.011% |
+| 7 | 12 | 0.033% |
+| 8 | 3 | 0.008% |
+| 100 | 74 | 0.201% |
+
+[DERIVED] Empty sets and singletons are 28,997/36,788 = 78.822% of the
+full evaluation support. They are not optimizer rows: the declared head returns
+zero without calling its network for `|A| <= 1`. The actual scalar-fit support
+is 7,791 rows with `|A| >= 2`; 7,104/7,791 = 91.181% of those rows are pairs.
+Thus the full support is dominated by trivial structural zeros and even the
+nontrivial support is dominated by pairs. Full-support fit statistics cannot be
+read as broad evidence about large coalitions. I therefore report the requested
+full-catalogue metrics and an explicit `|A| >= 2` sensitivity beside them.
+
+[RUN] Before fitting, all 28,960 singleton targets were exactly zero (maximum
+absolute value `0.0`); all 37 empty targets were also exactly zero. The maximum
+absolute residual in the normalized identity
+`joint/kappa - additive/kappa - Psi_A/kappa` was `2.8422e-14` over all 36,788
+candidates.
+
+## Answer
+
+[RUN] The declared target is only **weakly and metric-dependently learnable** on
+the repaired schema. V2 LOAO ordering is above chance and its bootstrap interval
+excludes 0.5, but level `R²` is negative and its interval crosses zero. Top-1 is
+`0.3243`, only `+0.0270` above the anchor-respecting constant floor, with
+overlapping intervals. The two-world LOWO check is more favorable for levels
+(`R² = 0.3328`) but full-support ordering is `0.4913`; removing the structural
+zero stratum changes that ordering to `0.5578`.
+
+[INFERRED] This is not a clean “unlearnable” result, but it is not a robust
+positive learnability result either. The route contains transferable level
+information, while reliable within-anchor coalition selection remains weak.
+
+## Evidence labels and scope
+
+- `[RUN]` means verified by running the required interpreter against the current
+  exact-path code and generated rows.
+- `[DERIVED]` means arithmetic or algebra applied to run outputs and declarations.
+- `[INFERRED]` is the stated interpretation of those measurements.
+
+[RUN] This was a declared-target predictive-quality diagnostic only. It ran no
+production training, policy, acceptance test, or EE endpoint. Loss values are
+never evidence about EE, no loss is used as such here, and this report makes no
+EE claim. No sealed source, constant, schema, threshold, sign, seed, horizon,
+price, control law, or optimizer setting was changed.
+
+## Sealed v2 primary and v1 secondary
+
+[RUN] Brackets are 95% percentile anchor-bootstrap intervals. Deltas are v2
+minus v1 point estimates.
+
+| protocol / metric | sealed v2 `(64,64)` | sealed v1 `(64,64)` | delta |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| LOAO level `R²` | `-0.0685 [-0.6700, 0.3668]` | `0.1079 [-0.7157, 0.5221]` | `-0.1764` |
+| LOAO ordering | `0.5484 [0.5180, 0.5789]` | `0.5299 [0.5008, 0.5588]` | `+0.0185` |
+| LOAO top-1 | `0.3243 [0.1892, 0.4865]` | `0.2703 [0.1351, 0.4061]` | `+0.0541` |
+| LOWO level `R²` | `0.3328 [-0.2352, 0.5485]` | `0.1859 [-0.5902, 0.4846]` | `+0.1469` |
+| LOWO ordering | `0.4913 [0.4653, 0.5189]` | `0.5049 [0.4796, 0.5276]` | `-0.0136` |
+| LOWO top-1 | `0.3311 [0.2160, 0.4595]` | `0.2770 [0.1689, 0.3851]` | `+0.0541` |
+
+[INFERRED] The repaired Q1 coordinates do affect route 3, but not in the simple
+direction seen for C1REALV2. They improve sealed top-1 in both protocols and
+nontrivial ordering in both, strongly improve LOWO level transfer, and worsen
+LOAO level `R²`. A v1-only C3 verdict would therefore be incomplete, but v2 is
+not a uniform rescue.
+
+[RUN] Every interval in the primary comparison is a 2,000-replicate percentile
+anchor-bootstrap interval. The bootstrap samples the 37 anchor sufficient
+statistics with replacement and reconstructs pooled metrics. LOAO uses one
+sealed learner seed. LOWO reports the arithmetic mean over the same four sealed
+seeds used by C1REAL. LOWO has only two world folds and is descriptive evidence
+about these two worlds, not a powered population-of-worlds estimate.
+
+## What the singleton mass does to the metrics
+
+[RUN] These are point estimates for the v2 primary and its fair constant.
+
+| model / protocol | evaluated support | level `R²` | ordering | top-1 |
+|---|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| sealed LOAO | full catalogue | `-0.0685` | `0.5484` | `0.3243` |
+| sealed LOAO | `|A| >= 2` | `-0.0713` | `0.5797` | `0.3243` |
+| sealed LOWO | full catalogue | `0.3328` | `0.4913` | `0.3311` |
+| sealed LOWO | `|A| >= 2` | `0.3311` | `0.5578` | `0.3311` |
+| anchored constant LOAO | full catalogue | `0.0019` | `0.6266` | `0.2973` |
+| anchored constant LOAO | `|A| >= 2` | `-0.0006` | `0.5000` | `0.2973` |
+| anchored constant LOWO | full catalogue | `-0.0006` | `0.6266` | `0.2973` |
+| anchored constant LOWO | `|A| >= 2` | `-0.0031` | `0.5000` | `0.2973` |
+
+[DERIVED] The structure-aware constant is the fair constant floor for the
+declared object: it predicts exact zero at `|A| <= 1` and the training-fold mean
+on `|A| >= 2`. The unanchored literal-mean comparator is also shown to expose how
+much the hard anchor itself changes top-1 and ordering. The unconstrained
+literal-mean comparator has LOAO/LOWO top-1 `0.0000` because stable argmax picks
+the empty candidate; its ordering is `0.5000`. Its nontrivial-only top-1 is
+`0.2973`. The declared-anchor floor is therefore `0.2973`, not the artificially
+easy `0.0000` comparison.
+
+[INFERRED] The anchored constant's full ordering `0.6266` is higher than every
+learned model because the metric is dominated by comparisons between forced
+zeros and nontrivial values. Its nontrivial ordering is exactly chance. This is
+direct evidence that full-support ordering is misleading here; the sealed
+head's `0.5797`/`0.5578` nontrivial ordering is the meaningful ordering signal.
+
+## References and empirical capacity ceiling
+
+[RUN] Point estimates are below. Every result file also contains the requested
+2,000-replicate anchor-bootstrap interval for all three metrics; compact interval
+tables follow.
+
+| v2 model | LOAO `R²` | LOAO order | LOAO top-1 | LOWO `R²` | LOWO order | LOWO top-1 |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| literal constant | `-0.0001` | `0.5000` | `0.0000` | `-0.0007` | `0.5000` | `0.0000` |
+| anchored constant | `0.0019` | `0.6266` | `0.2973` | `-0.0006` | `0.6266` | `0.2973` |
+| scalar linear | `0.0365` | `0.5421` | `0.3243` | `0.3968` | `0.4988` | `0.2703` |
+| sealed `(64,64)` | `-0.0685` | `0.5484` | `0.3243` | `0.3328` | `0.4913` | `0.3311` |
+| widened `(128,128)` | — | — | — | `0.1999` | `0.5088` | `0.2365` |
+| high-capacity raw+`256,256` RF | `0.0488` | `0.5479` | `0.2703` | `0.4828` | `0.5133` | `0.2703` |
+
+| v1 model | LOAO `R²` | LOAO order | LOAO top-1 | LOWO `R²` | LOWO order | LOWO top-1 |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| anchored constant | `0.0019` | `0.6266` | `0.2973` | `-0.0006` | `0.6266` | `0.2973` |
+| scalar linear | `0.0647` | `0.5288` | `0.3243` | `0.3907` | `0.4962` | `0.2703` |
+| sealed `(64,64)` | `0.1079` | `0.5299` | `0.2703` | `0.1859` | `0.5049` | `0.2770` |
+| high-capacity raw+`256,256` RF | `-0.1146` | `0.5346` | `0.3243` | `0.4155` | `0.5200` | `0.2973` |
+
+[RUN] Bootstrap intervals for the v2 references not already shown in the sealed
+comparison are:
+
+| model / protocol | level `R²` interval | ordering interval | top-1 interval |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| anchored constant LOAO | `[-0.0022, 0.0037]` | `[0.5935, 0.6596]` | `[0.1622, 0.4324]` |
+| anchored constant LOWO | `[-0.0070, 0.0024]` | `[0.5935, 0.6596]` | `[0.1622, 0.4324]` |
+| linear LOAO | `[-1.0094, 0.7099]` | `[0.5168, 0.5689]` | `[0.1892, 0.4865]` |
+| linear LOWO | `[0.0250, 0.6161]` | `[0.4721, 0.5281]` | `[0.1351, 0.4054]` |
+| widened `(128,128)` LOWO | `[-0.5251, 0.4912]` | `[0.4839, 0.5330]` | `[0.1351, 0.3446]` |
+| high-capacity LOAO | `[-0.9469, 0.6975]` | `[0.5235, 0.5730]` | `[0.1351, 0.4054]` |
+| high-capacity LOWO | `[0.1459, 0.6384]` | `[0.4974, 0.5302]` | `[0.1419, 0.4056]` |
+
+[RUN] For v1 linear, the LOAO intervals are `R² [-0.9280,0.7091]`, ordering
+`[0.5021,0.5553]`, top-1 `[0.1892,0.4865]`; LOWO gives
+`[0.0165,0.6100]`, `[0.4670,0.5269]`, `[0.1351,0.4054]`. For v1
+high capacity, LOAO gives `[-1.3708,0.6914]`, `[0.5122,0.5571]`,
+`[0.1892,0.4595]`; LOWO gives `[0.0349,0.6015]`, `[0.4997,0.5415]`,
+`[0.1622,0.4392]`. The sealed v1 intervals are in the primary table.
+
+[RUN] The linear reference standardizes each coordinate using outer-training
+rows, selects ridge from `{0.01,0.1,1,10,100,1000}` on training-only held-in
+anchors, and refits on the complete outer-training fold. The high-capacity
+reference is the C1REAL family adapted to scalar C3: standardized raw inputs
+plus fixed-seed `256,256` ReLU random features and an intercept, with the same
+training-only ridge grid. Both consume the same invariant vectors and receive
+the same hard-zero insertion at `|A| <= 1`.
+
+[RUN] The width screen preserves two ReLU hidden layers, 2,000 full-batch Adam
+epochs, learning rate `1e-3`, betas `(0.9,0.999)`, epsilon `1e-8`, zero weight
+decay, and direct scalar MSE. Width `(64,64)` is sealed; `(128,128)` is a
+diagnostic widening. The completed LOWO width screen regressed from sealed
+`(R², order, top-1) = (0.3328, 0.4913, 0.3311)` to
+`(0.1999, 0.5088, 0.2365)`. Because widening did not help and the separate
+`256,256` high-capacity basis was evaluated under both LOAO and LOWO, no wider
+Adam LOAO sweep was used to select a result.
+
+[INFERRED] The ceiling is **mixed**. For level calibration it is partly
+architectural/optimization-limited: on the same v2 inputs, the high-capacity
+reference changes LOAO `R²` from the sealed head's `-0.0685` to `0.0488` and
+LOWO from `0.3328` to `0.4828`; linear also beats the sealed head on both level
+checks. For selection it looks informational: no same-input model exceeds
+top-1 `0.3243`, only `0.0270` above the anchored constant; high capacity falls
+to `0.2703`, and widening falls to `0.2365`. Nontrivial ordering tops out at
+`0.5797` (sealed LOAO), while the high-capacity reference is `0.5656`.
+Therefore capacity can recover some levels but does not recover reliable
+argmax choice from these inputs.
+
+## Same-sample exact construction
+
+[RUN] The modeled panel mirrors C1REALV2: world 1 steps 0–17 and world 2 steps
+0–18, 37 anchors total, setting `a-r0`, carrier `nearest-eligible`, 100 users,
+the shipped bounded catalogue, unchanged calibration, and boundary `(0,)`.
+Generation took mean `386.6643`, median `374.2304`, and range
+`329.4410`–`535.7481` seconds per anchor, including exact source and catalogue
+work.
+
+[RUN] For every generation process, the imported pilot module's
+`PILOT_PRIMITIVE_SOURCE_FALLBACK` began `True`, was set to `False` in-process
+before `_build_anchor_rows`, and was restored to `True` in `finally`. The
+bounded catalogue was then enumerated by `_catalogue_with_census`, and
+`_exact_interactions` supplied exact normalized `joint`, `additive`, and `Psi`
+values. Generation held and released one anchor's source/evaluator rows at a
+time. The catalogue census reports zero candidate-shortlist misses and zero
+shortlist-superset misses at every anchor.
+
+[RUN] A C3-specific construction correction was necessary. The declared route
+state is `_route_state(row, "C3") = (*row.q1_state, *row.q2_state)`, while the
+pilot `_coalition_context` currently places Q1 alone in each member. The fitted
+diagnostic contexts preserve that function's physical/resource fields but put
+Q1+Q2 into both selected and incumbent member states. V2 repairs both Q1 parts
+through `mcrl-v025-stagec-q1-action-v2` and leaves Q2 unchanged; v1 retains the
+original Q1+Q2. This is why the observed member widths are 80 (v2) and 82 (v1),
+and invariant-vector dimensions are 324 (v2) and 328 (v1).
+
+[RUN] Production `CoalitionRow` deliberately rejects `|A| < 2`. To evaluate the
+declared full support without inventing invalid production rows, compact
+diagnostic records carry exact targets/sizes for all candidates, while complete
+`CoalitionContext` vectors are constructed only for the 7,791 trainable rows.
+This is a genuine C3 deviation from C1's per-action row construction. C3 also
+uses direct scalar MSE rather than C1's pairwise/gauge objective; no C1 pair cap
+or gauge was imported.
+
+[RUN] Source generation used the sealed eight-action selection shortlist because
+that is the support consumed by the bounded catalogue; it did not generate the
+2,000 off-selection legal actions per anchor that the catalogue census records
+as outside support. This avoids off-support exact work without omitting a
+catalogue candidate: each anchor has zero selection-shortlist and superset
+misses. This differs from the source-only research note's conservative
+`full_legal_actions=True` suggestion, not from the fitted bounded support.
+
+## Learner and metric protocol
+
+[RUN] The sealed primary is the repository `AdamMLPHead` wrapped with the
+declared `AdamSetInteractionHead` hard-zero semantics: hidden `(64,64)`, ReLU,
+learning rate `1.0e-3`, Adam betas `(0.9,0.999)`, epsilon `1e-8`, zero weight
