index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3dab23fdb1dbe4d04978dfca057d3acf0316a351
--- /dev/null
+++ b/C3-DECLARED-TARGET-LEARNABILITY-2026-09-10.md
@@ -0,0 +1,302 @@
+**On repaired v2, the sealed C3 head's LOAO ordering is `0.5484` (`0.5797` on `|A|>=2`), level `R²` is `-0.0685`, and top-1 is `0.3243` versus the anchor-respecting constant floor `0.2973`; the catalogue sizes are `{0:37, 1:28,960, 2:7,104, 3:292, 4:177, 5:125, 6:4, 7:12, 8:3, 100:74}`, and the empirical ceiling is mixed—architectural/optimization-limited for level calibration but informational-looking for coalition selection.**
+
+`DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`
+
+## Structural result before model statistics
+
+[RUN] The exact bounded catalogue contains 36,788 candidates at 37 anchors.
+The coalition-size distribution is:
+
+| `|A|` | rows | share of full catalogue |
+|---:|---:|---:|
+| 0 | 37 | 0.101% |
+| 1 | 28,960 | 78.721% |
+| 2 | 7,104 | 19.311% |
+| 3 | 292 | 0.794% |
+| 4 | 177 | 0.481% |
+| 5 | 125 | 0.340% |
+| 6 | 4 | 0.011% |
+| 7 | 12 | 0.033% |
+| 8 | 3 | 0.008% |
+| 100 | 74 | 0.201% |
+
+[DERIVED] Empty sets and singletons are 28,997/36,788 = 78.822% of the
+full evaluation support. They are not optimizer rows: the declared head returns
+zero without calling its network for `|A| <= 1`. The actual scalar-fit support
+is 7,791 rows with `|A| >= 2`; 7,104/7,791 = 91.181% of those rows are pairs.
+Thus the full support is dominated by trivial structural zeros and even the
+nontrivial support is dominated by pairs. Full-support fit statistics cannot be
+read as broad evidence about large coalitions. I therefore report the requested
+full-catalogue metrics and an explicit `|A| >= 2` sensitivity beside them.
+
+[RUN] Before fitting, all 28,960 singleton targets were exactly zero (maximum
+absolute value `0.0`); all 37 empty targets were also exactly zero. The maximum
+absolute residual in the normalized identity
+`joint/kappa - additive/kappa - Psi_A/kappa` was `2.8422e-14` over all 36,788
+candidates.
+
+## Answer
+
+[RUN] The declared target is only **weakly and metric-dependently learnable** on
+the repaired schema. V2 LOAO ordering is above chance and its bootstrap interval
+excludes 0.5, but level `R²` is negative and its interval crosses zero. Top-1 is
+`0.3243`, only `+0.0270` above the anchor-respecting constant floor, with
+overlapping intervals. The two-world LOWO check is more favorable for levels
+(`R² = 0.3328`) but full-support ordering is `0.4913`; removing the structural
+zero stratum changes that ordering to `0.5578`.
+
+[INFERRED] This is not a clean “unlearnable” result, but it is not a robust
+positive learnability result either. The route contains transferable level
+information, while reliable within-anchor coalition selection remains weak.
+
+## Evidence labels and scope
+
+- `[RUN]` means verified by running the required interpreter against the current
+  exact-path code and generated rows.
+- `[DERIVED]` means arithmetic or algebra applied to run outputs and declarations.
+- `[INFERRED]` is the stated interpretation of those measurements.
+
+[RUN] This was a declared-target predictive-quality diagnostic only. It ran no
+production training, policy, acceptance test, or EE endpoint. Loss values are
+never evidence about EE, no loss is used as such here, and this report makes no
+EE claim. No sealed source, constant, schema, threshold, sign, seed, horizon,
+price, control law, or optimizer setting was changed.
+
+## Sealed v2 primary and v1 secondary
+
+[RUN] Brackets are 95% percentile anchor-bootstrap intervals. Deltas are v2
+minus v1 point estimates.
+
+| protocol / metric | sealed v2 `(64,64)` | sealed v1 `(64,64)` | delta |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| LOAO level `R²` | `-0.0685 [-0.6700, 0.3668]` | `0.1079 [-0.7157, 0.5221]` | `-0.1764` |
+| LOAO ordering | `0.5484 [0.5180, 0.5789]` | `0.5299 [0.5008, 0.5588]` | `+0.0185` |
+| LOAO top-1 | `0.3243 [0.1892, 0.4865]` | `0.2703 [0.1351, 0.4061]` | `+0.0541` |
+| LOWO level `R²` | `0.3328 [-0.2352, 0.5485]` | `0.1859 [-0.5902, 0.4846]` | `+0.1469` |
+| LOWO ordering | `0.4913 [0.4653, 0.5189]` | `0.5049 [0.4796, 0.5276]` | `-0.0136` |
+| LOWO top-1 | `0.3311 [0.2160, 0.4595]` | `0.2770 [0.1689, 0.3851]` | `+0.0541` |
+
+[INFERRED] The repaired Q1 coordinates do affect route 3, but not in the simple
+direction seen for C1REALV2. They improve sealed top-1 in both protocols and
+nontrivial ordering in both, strongly improve LOWO level transfer, and worsen
+LOAO level `R²`. A v1-only C3 verdict would therefore be incomplete, but v2 is
+not a uniform rescue.
+
+[RUN] Every interval in the primary comparison is a 2,000-replicate percentile
+anchor-bootstrap interval. The bootstrap samples the 37 anchor sufficient
+statistics with replacement and reconstructs pooled metrics. LOAO uses one
+sealed learner seed. LOWO reports the arithmetic mean over the same four sealed
+seeds used by C1REAL. LOWO has only two world folds and is descriptive evidence
+about these two worlds, not a powered population-of-worlds estimate.
+
+## What the singleton mass does to the metrics
+
+[RUN] These are point estimates for the v2 primary and its fair constant.
+
+| model / protocol | evaluated support | level `R²` | ordering | top-1 |
+|---|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| sealed LOAO | full catalogue | `-0.0685` | `0.5484` | `0.3243` |
+| sealed LOAO | `|A| >= 2` | `-0.0713` | `0.5797` | `0.3243` |
+| sealed LOWO | full catalogue | `0.3328` | `0.4913` | `0.3311` |
+| sealed LOWO | `|A| >= 2` | `0.3311` | `0.5578` | `0.3311` |
+| anchored constant LOAO | full catalogue | `0.0019` | `0.6266` | `0.2973` |
+| anchored constant LOAO | `|A| >= 2` | `-0.0006` | `0.5000` | `0.2973` |
+| anchored constant LOWO | full catalogue | `-0.0006` | `0.6266` | `0.2973` |
+| anchored constant LOWO | `|A| >= 2` | `-0.0031` | `0.5000` | `0.2973` |
+
+[DERIVED] The structure-aware constant is the fair constant floor for the
+declared object: it predicts exact zero at `|A| <= 1` and the training-fold mean
+on `|A| >= 2`. The unanchored literal-mean comparator is also shown to expose how
+much the hard anchor itself changes top-1 and ordering. The unconstrained
+literal-mean comparator has LOAO/LOWO top-1 `0.0000` because stable argmax picks
+the empty candidate; its ordering is `0.5000`. Its nontrivial-only top-1 is
+`0.2973`. The declared-anchor floor is therefore `0.2973`, not the artificially
+easy `0.0000` comparison.
+
+[INFERRED] The anchored constant's full ordering `0.6266` is higher than every
+learned model because the metric is dominated by comparisons between forced
+zeros and nontrivial values. Its nontrivial ordering is exactly chance. This is
+direct evidence that full-support ordering is misleading here; the sealed
+head's `0.5797`/`0.5578` nontrivial ordering is the meaningful ordering signal.
+
+## References and empirical capacity ceiling
+
+[RUN] Point estimates are below. Every result file also contains the requested
+2,000-replicate anchor-bootstrap interval for all three metrics; compact interval
+tables follow.
+
